                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. De
                            Long to Soyeshima
                        Tane-omi.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United
                                States Legation, Japan</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1872-12-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 21, 1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 135.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your dispatch advising me of the change made by your government
                    in its calendar, and to heartily congratulate you upon this reform, which, while
                    it gives your government a more convenient system, also serves to bespeak the
                    great antiquity of His Majesty’s throne. I am sure that all western states will
                    hail this action with great pleasure.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. E. DE LONG.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
